bie**To: manglaSubj: oddCc: sauron, bladeDate: Dec 13My goddess has a death shout that names the player and guild of the onewho killed it.  It does all the guilds correctly except for Thief.Is this a problem of the thief guild?  A thief killing it is called an adventurer by the shout.  Also, if I do an mguild adventurer when I'm a thief, it says I'm alreadyin the adventurers guild.  Please let me know how I can fix this :)Wilbie**mangla**To: wilbieSubj: Thief problem fixedCc: blade, sauron, kryllDate: Dec 13The thief soul declared the disguise variable, but never set itsinitial value to 1 instead of 0 so that when you query guildon a thief, it would default to adventurer. I just added an initialstatement in the reset that makes the variable 1 at clone time.This should fix your problem.-Mangla**wilbie**To: manglaSubj: thanks, but...Cc: bladeDate: Dec 14I was talking to Uglymouth about the problem, and he found thedisguise variable as well.  But he also made a good point that the thief killing the thing might not WANT to be found out.Not wanting to over-ride Blade's disguise feature, I was thinkingof maybe having it somehow query the guild they are disguised as.But I'd need a little help (from Blade maybe) since I'm notsure how...Let me know what you think about this.  Your solution seems cool, butat the same time, I don't wanna give away any thieves :)Wilbie**mangla**To: wilbieSubj: thief guild disguiseCc: bladeDate: Dec 15I fixed a bug in the thiefs, What oyu want to do is a plainole query_level() which you will return the disguised as guildif the thief is disguised, To ensure it IS a thief, you wouldhave to query_real_guild()  So you are on the right track.-Mangla**fritz**To: bladeSubj: circeDate: Dec 18hiya!Blade, Circe told me that my mail necesarry to unbanish her,so i think she should be unbanished, i guess she will remember thislong enough. (hehe she promised me EVERYTHING what ca